Z||000000||jlhuber||10-12-1999||09:07 PM||||once again, i have an '86 (or technically '86.5) gt with the auto tranny. i am going to put a 5spd getrag in it, but first want to hear from people who have already done this swap.  is it easy? what kind of problems have been found with installation?  i am also looking for the best rebuild kit i can buy.  i want to keep the stock fiero engine, but i am looking for a little more umph.  gm says that they can easily get  270hp from a normally aspired 60 degree v-6, but i think it was the 3.1 used in off-road racing applications.  thus a 3.1 stroker kit may be what i'm looking for?  anyway, i'm looking for the most hp from the fiero engine without using nitrous or a turbo, i will however go for a supercharger for there is no "turbo lag" with them.  ...suggestions?  ||||reg||7
Z||000001||superXmotorsports||10-12-1999||10:37 PM||||In my opinion you should definetly stroke it and go 30 over to a 3.2L.  I currently have a 3.2L stroker with about 215hp.  It's nice but the one I'm having built this winter will hopefully yield 250hp.  I'm going with TRW forged pistons, compucam, P&P heads, FOCOA headers, HKS intake, and a carbon-fiber exhaust canister (the last 2 from the import scene).  I have run 14.3 with my current setup and I am shooting for high 12's low 13's with a 50hp NOS on the new car.<BR>If your interested in the custom HKS intake contact me.  <BR>||||reg||2
